th1-surjection-curation-001+math1-bijection-curation-001+math1-union-curation-001+math1-proper-curation-001+math1-complement-curation-001+math1-complement-render-001+math1-division-curation-001+math1-reciprocal-curation-001+math1-inequality-curation-001+math1-inequality-feedback-001+math1-maximum-curation-001+math1-minimum-curation-001+math1-boundedset-curation-001+math1-endpoint-curation-001+audit-groups-20261027+topup-math-i-20261028+topup-math-ii-20261028+topup-pt-20261028+topup-math-iii-20261028","concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/conditional-cumulative-distribution-function.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/conditional-cumulative-distribution-function.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X$ and $Y$ have joint density $f_{X,Y}$, and let $0<f_Y(y)<\\infty$, where $f_Y$ is the marginal density of $Y$. How is $F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ defined?","options":["$\\int_{-\\infty}^x f_{X,Y}(t,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$","$\\int_{-\\infty}^x f_{X\\mid Y}(t\\mid y)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$","$\\mathbb{P}(X\\le x,Y\\le y)/\\mathbb{P}(Y\\le y)$","$f_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ itself"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"aa9bed971aa3062cd785ed0a","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why can $\\mathbb{P}(X\\le x\\mid Y=y)$ not be computed as $\\mathbb{P}(X\\le x,Y=y)/\\mathbb{P}(Y=y)$ for a continuous $Y$?","options":["Dependence prevents the elementary conditional-probability formula from applying.","The zero numerator forces the conditional probability to equal zero.","The zero denominator makes the elementary ratio undefined.","An unconditional probability must replace the intersection in the numerator."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a1fb37c521c4f48ac300c959","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Where differentiation is justified, what is $\\partial F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)/\\partial x$?","options":["$f_{X,Y}(x,y)$","$F_X(x)$","$f_Y(y)$","$f_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8cf5c9c00aaa3da67f7b4dc0","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For continuous $X$ and $Y$, a conditional CDF satisfies $F_{X\\mid Y}(5\\mid2)=0.7$. Which statement does this express?","options":["$\\mathbb{P}(X\\le5,\\,Y\\le2)=0.7$","$\\mathbb{P}(X\\le5\\mid Y=2)=0.7$","$\\mathbb{P}(X\\le5\\mid Y\\le2)=0.7$","$\\mathbb{P}(Y\\le2\\mid X=5)=0.7$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"014f15da46e196d6313698cb","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Given $Y=y$, $X$ has density $2x/y^2$ on $(0,y)$. What is $F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ for $0<x<y$?","options":["$x^2$","$2x/y^2$","$x^2/y^2$","$\\tfrac{x}{y}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"21b617c21e46d8347bb4394c","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A point $(X,Y)$ is uniform on the disc $x^2+y^2<1$. Given $Y=y$, $X$ is uniform on $(-\\sqrt{1-y^2},\\sqrt{1-y^2})$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X\\le0.4\\mid Y=0.6)$?","options":["$\\tfrac{2}{5}$","$\\tfrac{3}{4}$","$\\tfrac{7}{10}$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"703c3f82338143a2209611d2","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a fixed threshold $x$, must the dependence of $F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ on the conditioning value $y$ satisfy the properties of a CDF in $y$?","options":["Yes, since its values lie between zero and one.","Yes, since it is a CDF in $x$ for each fixed $y$.","No, since monotonicity and CDF limits in $y$ need not hold.","No, since its values can exceed one as $y$ varies."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4e9225e40ee1ec9b8f0fcc34","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X,Y$ have joint density $f_{X,Y}$ and joint CDF $F_{X,Y}(x,y)=\\mathbb{P}(X\\le x,Y\\le y)$. At a value with $0<f_Y(y)<\\infty$, assume differentiation in $y$ gives $\\partial F_{X,Y}(x,y)/\\partial y=\\int_{-\\infty}^x f_{X,Y}(t,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. Which formula gives $F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$?","options":["$\\dfrac{F_{X,Y}(x,y)}{F_Y(y)}$","$\\dfrac{\\partial F_{X,Y}(x,y)/\\partial x}{f_Y(y)}$","$\\dfrac{\\partial F_{X,Y}(x,y)/\\partial y}{f_Y(y)}$","$\\dfrac{\\partial F_{X,Y}(x,y)}{\\partial y}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e081ac8aab6675b5dc39adc5","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $Y$ have density $f_Y$ and a finite mean. Write $F_X$ for the marginal CDF of $X$. Which identity holds for every threshold $x$?","options":["$F_X(x)=F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid\\mathbb{E}[Y])$","$F_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$F_X(x)=\\sup_yF_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$","$F_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)f_Y(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d532d8cd99278e32e09a3ac6","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$ does not depend on $y$ for every $x$, what follows?","options":["$X$ and $Y$ are independent","$X$ and $Y$ have the same marginal distribution","$X$ is constant with probability one","$Y$ is a function of $X$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"498abbcdd1691f296c3436e8","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Given $Y=y$, $X$ is uniform on $(0,y)$, and $Y$ is uniform on $(1,3)$. Using the conditional CDFs, find $\\mathbb{P}(X\\le1)$.","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\tfrac{1}{3}$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}\\ln3$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6c88cae00e31d1b5eefa354a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Given $Y=y\\in(0,1)$, $X$ has conditional CDF $x^{1/y}$ on $(0,1)$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid Y=y]$?","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$y$","$\\dfrac{1}{1+y}$","$\\dfrac{y}{1+y}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f2227c65f0ff89a2325d1183","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_003_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X$ and $Y$ have a joint density and fix $y$ with $0<f_Y(y)<\\infty$. Which of the following functions of $x$ can be the conditional CDF $F_{X\\mid Y}(x\\mid y)$?","options":["$0$ for $x<0$ and $1-\\mathrm{e}^{-x}$ for $x\\ge0$","$0$ for $x<0$ and $1-\\tfrac{1}{2}\\mathrm{e}^{-x}$ for $x\\ge0$","$0$ for $x<0$ and $\\tfrac{1}{2}(1-\\mathrm{e}^{-x})$ for $x\\ge0$","$1$ for $x<0$ and $\\mathrm{e}^{-x}$ for $x\\ge0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d2a2a8c86ceec07c94e92442","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_014_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Given $Y=y>0$, $X$ is uniform on $(0,y^2)$. What is the conditional median of $X$ given $Y=2$?","options":["$1$","$2$","$4$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9652e33adce880a97fac9f10","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_conditional_cumulative_distribution_function_107bf435_015_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X=Y+Z$, where $Z\\sim\\operatorname{Exp}(1)$ is independent of $Y$, and let $Y$ have a density with $0<f_Y(1)<\\infty$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X>3\\mid Y=1)$?","options":["$\\mathrm{e}^{-3}$","$1-\\mathrm{e}^{-2}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{-1}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{-2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dcb27f51a0690f681acbcc97","time_limit":30}]}}